From 78747995c379660563577c0eeaaee8b90cb9422c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: max994-dev <bmax994@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:43:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Attach the signed authorization to CCPA emails; skip stub
 scan rows; daily log files
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- lib/broker_helpers.py: brokers may refuse an agent's request without the
  consumer's signed permission (11 CCR 7063 — Radaris and others do). The
  site now produces a signed PDF at onboarding; fetch it from
  AUTHORIZATION_PDF_URL (authenticated with the same PD_UPLOAD_SECRET header
  as the upload endpoints), cache it per user for 6h, and attach it to every
  CCPA/GDPR email as PrivacyDuck-Authorization.pdf. A user who has not
  signed (404) sends without it, exactly as before; a network failure logs
  and sends without it rather than blocking the request.

- manage.py: 408 of the 416 sites_scan modules are auto-generated stubs
  that raise ModuleNotFoundError. get_pending_scan fetched their rows
  regardless and marked each step=4 one at a time — about 0.3s a row, two
  minutes per user per rescan — and the five real scans (the free-scan
  flow) queued behind that churn. Restrict selection to domains with a real
  module, detected once per run; stub rows simply stay at step=0.

- manage.py: add a per-day log file (removal-daily.log.YYYY-MM-DD.log, kept
  14 days) beside the size-rotated removal.log. After a restart the rotated
  removal.log.1 looked like today's log but was the previous run's tail;
  with daily files "what happened on the 20th" is always one file. PD_LOG_DIR
  overrides the location.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
